# dotfiles-Fedora/.gitignore
*.log
*.bak
*.pre-dotfiles.*
.DS_Store
# Crash dumps. `core.[0-9]*` and NOT `core.*`: this repo tracks core.lock, and Core itself
# tracks core.manifest and core.version — a blanket rule would hide the next such file the
# moment someone added one, silently. Bare `core` is deliberately not matched either: that
# is the vendored Core DIRECTORY. Matches the kernel/glibc `core.<pid>` spelling.
core.[0-9]*
# ANCHORED (leading slash) on purpose. An unanchored `.claude/` matches at ANY depth, so it
# also swallowed core/.claude/ — 14 files that are TRACKED, because they arrive with the
# vendored subtree. The vendored core/ must byte-match upstream or core-integrity.sh's
# tree-SHA comparison fails, so a `git subtree pull` that needs to re-add one of those files
# must never be silently skipped by an ignore rule. Keep every repo-meta pattern rooted.
/.claude/

# ── secrets: nothing here is ever tracked ─────────────────────────────────────
# This repo stores NO secrets by design — runtime secrets come from 1Password via
# `op` (see core/zsh/50-op.zsh). These patterns are the belt-and-braces for the
# usual accidents: an .env dropped next to the configs, a key pasted into the tree,
# a credential file written by a tool. See SECURITY.md.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/*.pub
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
.npmrc
credentials.json
# host-local git identity (name/email) is SEEDED to ~/.config/git/local.gitconfig
# by bootstrap.sh and edited there — it must never be tracked back from this repo.
local.gitconfig

# private SSH material — deny-by-default, and nothing here is tracked any more.
# The ssh CLIENT CONFIG moved into Core (dotgibson/dotfiles-core#450): it is now
# core/ssh/config, symlinked by blib_link_core. Keep this rule: it means a key
# dropped under ssh/ is untracked unless someone deliberately allowlists it, which
# is the safe direction to be wrong in. An OS-specific ssh need is ssh/os.conf
# (linked to ~/.ssh/config.d/50-os.conf) and would need its own ! line here.
ssh/*
